.TH AD_LAYER_SPLIT_IN_PLACE 1 "2026-09-11" "ad 2.0" "ad layers"
.SH NAME
ad_layer_split_in_place \- insert content AFTER splitting lines (prevents concatenation)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ad_layer_split_in_place
< raw_ops > split_ops
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ad_layer_split_in_place
reorders the pattern:
.RS
.nf
insert(L, col 1, chars)+  \(->  split_line(L, K)
.fi
.RE
to:
.RS
.nf
split_line(L, col 1)  \(->  insert(L, col 1, chars)+
.fi
.RE
.PP
so the split happens FIRST (creating an empty line L, with the old
content moving to line L+1), then the inserts fill the empty line L.
Without this reorder, the inserted text and the old content are
momentarily concatenated on line L before the split separates them
\(em a visual "join then move" artifact.
.PP
Only matches when there IS old content on the line (detected by
checking if the op after the split_line is a
.B keep
or
.B keep_line
on line L+1). When the line is empty (e.g. end-of-file inserts),
the pattern is left unchanged.
.PP
Only matches full-line insertions (inserts starting at col 1).
Partial content at col > 1 is left unchanged.
.PP
Symmetric of
.BR ad_layer_line_delete_in_place .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help and exit.
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
V2 TSV format. Input should be raw compute output or post-reorder.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B ad_layer_split_in_place < raw_ops.txt > split_ops.txt
Reorder insert-then-split patterns.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ad_postprocess (1),
.BR ad_layer_line_delete_in_place (1),
.BR ad (1)
.PP
.I docs/src/plugin-layers.md
